%N A398993 The binomial matrix of the Bell numbers. Square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A398993 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A398993 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A398993 A(n, n) = B(n), the Bell numbers.
%F A398993 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * B(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
